.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd September 6, 2026
.Dt SYS-INIT-CHECK-HOST 1
.Os sys-init experimental
.Sh NAME
.Nm sys-init-check-host
.Nd run bounded trusted-child host fixtures
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm python3 scripts/check-host-runtime.py
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Run the real trusted-child host fixtures using Python 3.10 or newer on a POSIX
host, from the repository root.
The fixtures exercise the bounded host adapter;
they do not operate host services or execute native Aether images.
The command discovers test_host*.py modules and runs a worker in a fresh
session.
The parent requires a nonempty, complete, successful suite with no skipped
cases.
.Pp
The worker has a 30-second watchdog.
On timeout the parent kills the owned
process group containing trusted, non-detaching fixtures and exits with
failure.
Combined stdout/stderr capture is limited to 4 MiB of raw bytes.
Overflow kills the owned group, reaps the direct worker and fails the check.
The deadline includes pipe draining and process exit.
Worker allocations and child-created files are outside this limit.
This is not confinement against
arbitrary or untrusted child programs.
.Sh ARGUMENTS
There is no ordinary option parser, help mode, version mode or output option.
Any argument list other than the exact internal --suite-worker invocation is
ignored and starts the normal fixture run.
In particular, do not use --help,
--version or an unknown argument expecting a side-effect-free query.
.Pp
The exact --suite-worker invocation is an internal mode.
It directly runs the
suite and emits suite-count evidence, bypassing the parent watchdog and
summary.
Use the no-argument form for ordinary validation.
.Sh OUTPUT
Successful execution prints JSON on standard output with profile
trusted-host-children-v1, result pass, the observed test count, host/Python
identity, elapsed seconds and selected source hashes.
Unittest details are copied to standard error.
The standalone command does not create a retained report directory.
.Pp
A worker failure returns the worker's status without a parent success summary.
Rejected suite evidence or timeout produces a standard-error diagnostic and
exits 1.
Timeout or overflow replays the accepted stderr prefix before its diagnostic.
Partial stdout is discarded and cannot become a passing suite report.
Overflow also exits 1.
Interpreter or process-launch failure can produce a traceback instead.
Use the aggregate runner to retain the outer streams in a private run
directory.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
The worker uses the invoking Python executable and inherited environment;
its working directory is the repository root.
No command-specific environment configuration or network setup is provided.
Fixture code creates its own temporary workspaces and real child processes.
.Sh FILES
Tests are read from tests/test_host*.py and import the host adapter and model.
Temporary fixture artifacts follow the host's temporary-directory
configuration.
There is no output-directory operand or durable standalone report file.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 0
All discovered required tests passed and suite evidence was accepted.
.It 1
Parent watchdog expiry, rejected suite evidence or ordinary Python failure.
.It Other nonzero status
The parent propagates a nonzero worker status.
It does not normalize all
signal or interpreter outcomes to one documented numeric code.
.El
.Pp
There is no special usage-error or help-success exit contract.
Exceptions during capture, including Python KeyboardInterrupt, kill the owned
group and reap the direct child.
Abrupt external termination and detached nested groups have no such guarantee.
.Sh EXAMPLES
From the repository root on a supported POSIX host with Python provisioned:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
python3 scripts/check-host-runtime.py
.Ed
.Pp
Expect unittest detail on standard error and a passing JSON summary on
standard
output only when the required suite passes.
No root privileges are needed.
To retain logs, use the aggregate runner:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
python3 scripts/check-all.py
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
Repository guides: docs/HOST-RUNTIME.md, docs/DEVELOPMENT-CHECKS.md,
docs/QUALITY-PROCESS.md and docs/DOCUMENTATION-INVENTORY.md.
.Sh CAVEATS
The manual title is not an installed executable.
Independent review and target
manual lookup remain pending.
A pass applies to the recorded host and source,
not every POSIX system, PID 1 or native Aether behavior.
